<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Such joys as are unspeakable,</l><l>And full of glory too;</l><l>Such splendid riches, meat and drink,</l><l>As worldlings do not know.</l><l>Eye hath not seen, nor ear hath heard,</l><l>For fancy ’tis concealed,</l><l>What Thou, Lord, hast laid up for Thine</l><l>And hast to me revealed.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>I feel Thy touch, I hear Thy voice,</l><l>I taste Thy sweetest grace;</l><l>My soul doth leap: but, oh, that I</l><l>May see Thee face to face!</l><l>Then with the saints my soul shall feast</l><l>On joys that always last:</l><l>Blest be my God, the God of joy,</l><l>That gives here such a taste!</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
